# Storyloom — E2E test environment. Copy to `.env.e2e` and fill in.
#
# TEST-ONLY. Nothing under `src/` reads this file and nothing here ships in the
# app bundle. `.env.e2e` is gitignored; keep it that way.
#
# Why this exists: the project requires email confirmation (correct for
# production), so a programmatic sign-up gets a user with no session — and every
# sign-up burns one of the few emails an hour Supabase's built-in SMTP allows.
# A service-role client creates the test user already confirmed, so no mail is
# sent, no rate limit applies, and teardown can delete the account cleanly.
#
# Where to get it:
#   Supabase Dashboard -> your project -> Project Settings -> API Keys
#   -> `service_role` (the SECRET one, not `anon`)
#
# This key bypasses RLS entirely. It belongs here and in CI secrets, nowhere else.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
